<title>UK: Beta Finance sets $200 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>Beta Finance sets $200 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BETA FINANCE</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     6.75	MATURITY    28.APR.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.0975  PAY DATE    28.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.91     SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/KY</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.1875    SELL CONC  1.1875    PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT U.S. TREASURY DUE FEBRUARY 2000  NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
